Scene summary: Hook: the night before the monthly management meeting, the cluster lead sits alone in the meeting hall; tomorrow she must present her cluster's performance but the data is still scattered across program officers and she has no slides. The product does not appear. 9:16 vertical, realistic live-action, shot on a modern smartphone | Primary Video Type: UGC Native (PJ Klaster harus memaparkan kinerja klasternya di lokmin besok, slide belum ada) + Supporting Format: Product Demo | Locked-off medium shots in an empty puskesmas meeting hall at night lit by a projector; one close-up of the laptop; Seq 3 single static tripod medium shot at the front table. REFERENCE PRIORITY: Use DNA Character as the authority for the talent's FACE and BODY identity only (not the outfit). Use DNA Product as the authority for the exact product identity. WARDROBE below overrides any outfit visible in the DNA Character image. CHARACTER LOCK: Use the DNA Character reference ONLY for the talent's face and body identity: exact face shape, jawline, skin tone, eye shape, eyebrows, hair or hijab style, body proportions and distinguishing features. Do NOT copy the outfit from the reference image; the outfit is defined in WARDROBE below. Keep the exact same face and body throughout the sequence. Do not add accessories or name tags not listed in WARDROBE. WARDROBE (OVERRIDES REFERENCE OUTFIT): Mustard-yellow instant hijab, white long-sleeve tunic, dark navy cardigan, black long skirt, flat black shoes, simple brown watch. No uniform badge, no name tag, no lanyard. PRODUCT LOCK: Exact Kit PKP Puskesmas 2026 per Klaster ILP package from the DNA Product reference image (the real package mockup uploaded as an ingredient). Preserve the exact box colors, title text, cover design, proportions and visible design details exactly as in the reference. Do NOT invent a different box design. It may appear with a printed annual PKP report example in a clear folder, and a laptop showing the package's tools: an Excel sheet of monthly achievement per cluster with a line chart, a ranked list of the largest gaps highlighted in red, and a slide deck for a cluster performance presentation (charts only, no readable text). Do not redesign, simplify, recolor, or rebrand the box. SET & PROPS: Empty puskesmas meeting hall at night: a blank white projector screen lit by a projector beam, rows of plastic chairs, a front table with a laptop and a few loose printed recap sheets (no readable text), ceiling lights half off, quiet, no other people. TIMELINE — 10 seconds: 0–2s Hook · close-up: the blank projector screen glowing white; cut to medium shot of her at the front table as she looks to the camera. VO (ID, verbatim): "Besok saya paparan di lokmin." Delivery (EN): calm, slightly tense 2–4s Problem · medium shot, she picks up a few loose recap sheets. VO (ID, verbatim): "Kinerja klaster bulan ini." Delivery (EN): honest 4–6s Problem · medium close-up, she shuffles the sheets, each in a different layout. VO (ID, verbatim): "Datanya masih dari tiap pengelola." Delivery (EN): concerned 6–8s Problem · medium shot, she gestures at the blank screen. VO (ID, verbatim): "Slide-nya belum ada sama sekali." Delivery (EN): worried 8–10s Beat · medium shot, she sets the sheets down and exhales. VO: none. AUDIO: Quiet hall ambience at night, projector fan hum, a clock ticking. Only the talent speaks. Natural Indonesian, conversational, clear pronunciation, no background music. Lighting/mood: realistic natural light matching the set, clean soft contrast, believable Indonesian setting, not glossy, not studio. Camera: follow the camera style above consistently; stable and restrained, no whip pans, no drone, no 360 orbit. Keep product readable whenever it is on screen. Performance: natural facial expression, believable professional UGC, natural eye contact, restrained gestures, no exaggerated acting. Lips clearly synced to each word. Hands: simple, natural, relaxed movements. CLEAN OUTPUT: No subtitles, captions, generated text overlays, watermark, poster layout, storyboard panels, or added graphics. Do not invent product details, claims, prices, ratings, testimonials, certifications, or guarantees. Keep exact talent face, the WARDROBE above, product shape, colors, packaging, box, printed report, laptop screen, laptop screen content, and visual details consistent with the DNA references.